 "scribe_vocals_2": {
  "text": "Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration, along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe. Motion, motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run. Sleeping, air moves into and out of our lungs. Blood flows in arteries and veins. Carry people, automobiles, and planes. Water flowing down a dam. Leaves falling from trees. Motion, motion, change in position object with time. Velocity, acceleration, on a straight line. The sun, the sun, in motion in the Milky Way, Milky Way. Moving within its local group of galaxiiiies. Rectilinear motion, uniform acceleration, a set of simple equations. Relative nature of motion, relative velocity. Point objects valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations, size neglected without much error. Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration, along a straight line.",
